                                <h1 class="page-title">Data downloads</h1>
                <div class="entry-content">
                    
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This page contains the Open Repair Alliance dataset of open repair data available for download.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We provide an aggregate dataset of all datasets combined together, as well as links to locations of individual datasets from partner organisations.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you&#8217;d like to collect repair data yourself, you can <a href="https://openrepair.org/how-to-get-started/">learn how to record repair data here</a>.  Have you already used the Open Repair Alliance data?  <a href="https://therestartproject.typeform.com/to/wfEGJB3i">Fill in our survey</a> to give us your thoughts and feedback.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-css-opacity"/>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Full open repair data dataset</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Summary</strong><br>This is the full Open Repair Alliance dataset, contained a row-by-row CSV of EEE repair attempts logged and a summary of non-EEE repair attempts, all logged by repair groups around the world and shared by <a href="https://openrepair.org/members/">ORA partner organisations</a>. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Record count:</strong><br>305,649 rows of EEE data.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Published by:</strong><br>The Open Repair Alliance</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Data last updated:</strong><br>October 2025 (including data to end of July 2025)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Structure:</strong><br><a href="https://standard.openrepair.org" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">ORDS v0.3</a></p>



